From ac55709a7e7bba5117842460b07ddbf277f7c0d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 53/59] domainset: the names of rule-sets in a compact trie

The domain matcher of rule-sets built with a fraction of the memory of sing's: a trie whose levels
are keys one after another and a bit a node, read from the source format in one pass, on 32-bit
architectures too.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  29834ed30 common/domainset: build the domain matcher of sing with a fraction of its memory
  046b5ba9e domainset: read rule sets of the source format in one pass, build the trie by radix
  a53ff309b domainset: a level of the trie is its keys one after another and a bit a node
  677cfdad7 domainset: the trie a type of its own, filled in place
  dcee4dfd3 domainset: build on 32-bit architectures
  e1021c0bf domainset: a name and a suffix of one key are one key, as in sing v0.9.7
  2c49493bd domainset: ReadSourceAddresses reads a rule set without building its names

Pdk-Feature: domainset
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 04
